---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="WalkPath collects no personal data. Here is exactly what runs in your browser and which third parties see job text." current="about">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      WalkPath needs no account, has no email list and uploads no resume. We do not collect, store
      or sell personal data. This page lists everything that happens in your browser, the optional
      account, and every third party involved.
    </p>

    <h2>In your browser</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Saved and applied jobs</strong> are kept in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>
        under <code>walkpath:tracker</code>, along with the time of your last visit. Nothing is sent to us.
        The Saved page offers an export, an import and a "clear my data" button.
      </li>
      <li><strong>No cookies</strong>, no fingerprinting, no third-party embeds.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Optional account</h2>
    <p>
      If this deployment has accounts enabled, you can sign in with Google or an emailed link to sync
      your saved jobs and profile across devices. Sign-in and storage are provided by Google Firebase
      (Authentication and Cloud Firestore), which acts as our processor. The account stores exactly
      two things: your tracker (job ids, stage, date, your note) and your profile (graduation year,
      degree, majors, skills, preferences). No resume file is ever uploaded. Only you can read or
      write your document. The Account page has a "Delete my account" button that removes the stored
      document and the sign-in; see <code>docs/accounts.md</code> in the repository for the rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and serves its files. Cloudflare Web Analytics
        (cookie-less, no personal identifiers) counts page views.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Brandfetch</strong> serves company logos from its CDN; your browser requests a logo
        image by company domain. If the logo service is not configured, a letter avatar is shown instead.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Mistral, Google (Gemini) and Cloudflare Workers AI</strong> receive public job-posting
        text from our pipeline to generate summaries. This runs on our side, never from your browser,
        and never involves anything about you. Those providers may use free-tier prompts to improve
        their models; only public posting text is sent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub</strong> hosts the source code, the published data and the "report a listing"
        issue form. Opening an issue is subject to GitHub's own privacy policy.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Apply links</h2>
    <p>
      Clicking Apply sends you to the employer's own careers page. Links are sent with a
      <code>strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code> referrer policy, so the employer sees that you came
      from this site but not which page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions go to the project's <a href="https://github.com/alterj07/walkpath/issues" rel="noopener">issue tracker</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
